  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLIMATE CHANGE AND SUSTAINABLE FOOD SYSTEMS WITH AN INTEGRAL ECOLOGY APPROACH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CENDA&apos;s project will contribute to the strengthening, through an integral ecology approach, of community life systems, resilient to the impacts of climate change, in the Sacaba municipality, to serve as a benchmark for territorial and environmental management in other communities.
CENDA will work directly a community located in a peri-urban area outside of Cochabamba city, home to indigenous campesino families. The communities in this region are surviving in a context marked by the ever-increasing impacts of climate change, increasing costs of food and goods for food production (fertilizers, pesticides and fuel) and increasing social conflict over access to water.  The project will bring together the three strands of work that CENDA supports: agroecological food production and agroforestry, water resource management and territorial management and leadership support. CENDA intend to work with the community integrating each strand of work, bringing together for the first time, their separate teams&#x2019; expertise</narrative>
  </description>
